    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "If the radius is doubled, how is the arc length changed to keep the angle the same?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "It doubles, since $s=r\\theta$ with $\\theta$ fixed means that $s$ varies directly with $r$.",
      "worked": "The ratio $\\theta=\\frac{l}{r}$ must stay the same. Doubling both $l$ and $r$ keeps this ratio unchanged, so the arc length doubles.",
